# Release Control Support Makefiles

These makefiles provide a framework for building Darwin Core OS
projects under Release Control.  The original sources are placed in a
subdirectory of the project and wrapped with a small makefile that
drops the project into the framework.

- `Common.make` provides the core functionality following the RC
  makefile API.  It implements the `installsrc` and `clean` targets and
  defines the dependencies between all of the standard targets,
  including `build` and `install`.

- `GNUSource.make` implements the `build` and `install` targets for
  sources which use a GNU autoconf `configure` script to build.

- `BSDCommon.make` implements the `build` and `install` targets for
  Apple-style projects (tools, dylibs, and static libraries) presented
  to Release Control as `ProductType`.

This tree is a clean-room reimplementation of Apple's Release Control
support makefiles and preserves their public interface (variable
names, targets, and defaults) so that Darwin projects build
unmodified.  Not affiliated with Apple.